BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art at the Kent 2026: Throughlines
DTSTART:20261011T100000
DTEND:20261011T170000
DTSTAMP:20261016T152432Z
UID:4304fa6bc336806c668265abe82e0f@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Art at the Kent’s widely anticipated 2026 exhibition\, Throu
 ghlines \, gathers the work of 20 contemporary Vermont artists from Friday
 \, September 11\, through Sunday\, October 11\, 2026. Visitors can view th
 ese works within the rambling historic structures of the Kents’ Corner S
 tate Historic Site—as well as on the surrounding grounds. With multidisc
 iplinary works of art reflecting themes of place\, community\, and connect
 ion\, Throughlines celebrates the making of art using myriad materials and
  many ways of seeing\, key characteristics at the heart of our exhibitions
  for the past two decades. Various interpretations of the theme\, both ove
 rt and subtle\, are evidenced in the diverse work of the exhibiting artist
 s. In Throughlines\, marks made in one medium evoke rich relationships wit
 h those made in another\, deepening the viewer’s appreciation for resona
 nce. Throughout the Kent\, with its own storied patina tying the present t
 o the past\, the connections made between art and building and visitor ech
 o the ties between time and place and community as our audience discovers 
 a unique sense of shared roots and different perspectives. Creative expres
 sion becomes a throughline for appreciating life’s odysseys\, preserving
  a sense of possibility\, and navigating the way forward. Art at the Kent 
 also hosts a variety of associated events that visitors can experience\, i
 ncluding Words Out Loud\, the popular Sunday afternoon reading series (Sep
 tember 13\, 20\, and 27) at the historic meetinghouse nearby\, the Old Wes
 t Church. All programs can be found on the website including multiple arti
 st talks\, demonstrations of mokuhanga (a Japanese printmaking technique) 
 and paper folding\, as well as a presentation on the history and repair of
  antique typewriters. More information and a full listing of these and oth
 er events can be found on the Art at the Kent Events page. Art at the Kent
  is a program of Historic Kents’ Corner\, Inc.\, in partnership with the
  Vermont State Curator’s Office and the Vermont Division for Historic Pr
 eservation. For nearly two decades\, contemporary art exhibitions have bee
 n presented to engage and challenge audiences by providing unusual exposur
 e to mid-nineteenth-century architecture enhanced by the art of our time. 
 The Kents’ Corner State Historic Site is administered by the Vermont Div
 ision for Historic Preservation. Open to all. Donations encouraged. Exhibi
 tion Dates: September 11–October 11\, 2026 Every week through Oct 11\, 2
 026.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Kents’ Corner State Historic Site\, 7 Old West Church Rd
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/art-at-the
 -kent-2026-throughlines-07-08-2026-11-38-46
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Brattleboro House Concert: The Hayden Stern Band
DTSTART:20261016T190000
DTEND:20261016T210000
DTSTAMP:20261016T152432Z
UID:b75fa7a00791909a2164e2d21acb7a@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:As a fiddler\, composer\, and community builder Hayden Stern h
 as taken Seattle’s roots music scene by storm. Stern draws freely from m
 ultiple traditions\, expanding his original base of Scottish fiddling to I
 rish\, Scandinavian\, French-Canadian\, Appalachian\, and beyond. The mate
 rial from his debut album\, The Morning Dark\, focuses on his own composit
 ions\, bringing his roving ear and keen focus on arranging to a live perfo
 rmance built to rouse everyone to dance. Coming originally from Santa Cruz
 \, California’s rich roots music scene\, Stern grew up attending Scottis
 h fiddle camps\, immersing himself in tradition at an early age. Shortly a
 fter arriving in Seattle\, he discovered contra dancing\, and with it a ne
 w community of like-minded LGBTQ musicians and dancers. He’s been captiv
 ating listening rooms and dancefloors across the US ever since. As The Hay
 den Stern Band\, he is joined by powerhouse musicians Molly Tucker (fiddle
 \, viola) and Ezra Jane Landsman (guitar). Together\, they play a mix of t
 raditional repertoire and original compositions from Hayden’s debut albu
 m\, The Morning Dark. FACEBOOK EVENT PAGE: https://www.facebook.com/events
 /1782681412888211/ Under the Maple Suggestion donation $20-$30\; any amoun
 t welcome\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Vermont Public is independent\, community-supported media\, servi
 ng Vermont with trusted\, relevant and essential information. We share sto
 ries that bring people together\, from every corner of our region.\, © 20
 26 Vermont Public | 365 Troy Ave. Colchester\, VT 05446
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/brattlebor
 o-house-concert-the-hayden-stern-band-11-08-2026-20-15-22
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Champlain Valley Craft Show & Antique Expo
DTSTART:20261016T100000
DTEND:20261016T170000
DTSTAMP:20261016T152432Z
UID:e12fa90b1ff6c606f2267d4df25b80@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Peak foliage. Community spirit. Timeless finds. Join us for th
 e Champlain Valley Craft Show & Antique Expo\, October 16–18 at the Cham
 plain Valley Exposition in Essex Junction — a beloved fall tradition in 
 the heart of Vermont. Recently voted Best Craft Fair by Seven Days readers
 \, this long-running autumn event brings together exceptional handmade art
 istry\, vintage treasures\, and live demonstrations during one of the most
  beautiful seasons in the Green Mountain State. What you’ll discover: 
 • Over 125 booths of juried arts\, crafts\, specialty foods & antiques 
 • Handcrafted work from talented regional artisans • Carefully curated
  antiques\, collectibles & timeless décor • Live craft demonstrations 
 • A spacious indoor setting with acres of free parking For shoppers who 
 value the arts and appreciate work made with care and character\, this wee
 kend offers something truly meaningful. It’s a gathering of craftsmanshi
 p\, creativity\, and history — set against the beauty of Vermont in autu
 mn. Show Hours Friday\, October 16: 10am – 5pm Saturday\, October 17: 10
 am – 5pm Sunday\, October 18: 10am – 4pm Admission: $12 per adult Chil
 dren under 14 are free Tickets valid all three days Indoor event — rain
 \, snow\, or shine Champlain Valley Exposition 105 Pearl St.\, Essex Junct
 ion\, VT 05452 Directions: From I-89 take Exit 11. More information (inclu
 ding discount coupon): CastleberryFairs.com\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Champlain Valley Expo\, 105 Pearl St
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/champlain-
 valley-craft-show-antique-expo-10-10-2026-10-46-13
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Colin McCaffrey and Jim Rooney Present: Pat Alger
DTSTART:20261016T190000
DTEND:20261016T210000
DTSTAMP:20261016T152432Z
UID:72b123e6b783014ed3e738ec8eaa6f@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:The McCaffrey & Rooney Present series starts up again on Frida
 y\, October 16\, with a not to be missed concert of songs and stories by l
 egendary Nashville singer/songwriter Pat Alger joined by Jim Rooney and Co
 lin McCaffrey. Pat Alger’s songs have been recorded by dozens of artists
  in different genres including The Everly Brothers\, Brenda Lee\, Peter\, 
 Paul & Mary\, Nanci Griffith\, Dolly Parton\, Livingston & James Taylor\, 
 Don Williams\, Ian Tyson\, Kathy Mattea\, Hal Ketchum\, Trisha Yearwood an
 d Garth Brooks. Some of Pat’s best-known songs are “Once In A Very Blu
 e Moon\,” “Goin’ Gone\,” “Small Town Saturday Night\,” “True
  Love\,” “Like We Never Had A Broken Heart\,” “Unanswered Prayers
 \,” and “The Thunder Rolls.” In 1991\, Pat became the Nashville Song
 writers Association International “Songwriter of the Year”. The follow
 ing year he was ASCAP’s “Country Songwriter of the Year.” In 2010\, 
 Pat was inducted into the Nashville Songwriters Hall of Fame\, and in 2013
  he became one of only a handful of songwriters elected to the Georgia Mus
 ic Hall of Fame. ​ Middlebury College\, 72 Porter Field Road Middlebury 
 \, Vermont 05753 8027632334 sevenstarsarts@gmail.com https://www.sevenstar
 sarts.org/ Submit An Event Find out what's happening in your neck of the w
