BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Music in the Gallery-Benjii Aresty
DTSTART:20261016T130000
DTEND:20261016T140000
DTSTAMP:20261016T152432Z
UID:f298b074141e32eb0b6236e0178769@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Join us in the splendid setting of the 19th-century Art Galler
 y for our Music Series with Benji Aresty. American-born songwriter and vis
 ionary Benji Aresty brings his rising independent music project to the Ath
 enaeum. With a voice that’s lived many lives and lyrics that cut straigh
 t to the heart\, Benji writes songs that feel like soul medicine—raw\, r
 eal\, and meant to move you. The music spans folk\, blues\, soul\, and cin
 ematic rock\, grounded in live instrumentation and emotional storytelling.
  Benji’s songwriting is deeply personal\, often born from grief\, love\,
  transformation\, and spiritual inquiry. His lyrics are a call to feel mor
 e\, to heal more\, and to live more aligned with truth. Whether it’s an 
 acoustic ballad or an electrifying anthem\, each song is created with purp
 ose: to open hearts\, spark conversations\, and create moments of collecti
 ve resonance. Aresty. isn’t just about sound—it’s about soul. The pr
 oject’s mission is to use music as a tool for emotional and social awake
 ning. Its vision reaches beyond entertainment\, aiming to build community
 \, raise consciousness\, and be a bridge between cultures. In a time when 
 the world is aching for authenticity and healing\, Aresty. is showing up w
 ith open arms\, a full band\, and a message that matters. Listeners of Ray
  LaMontagne\, The Head The Heart\, John Mayer and Michael Franti will enjo
 y Aresty. Aresty. is on a journey—one rooted in integrity\, driven by in
 tention\, and uplifted by the power of song. Listen to Unconditional Lovin
 g - https://aresty.bandcamp.com/track/unconditional-loving This event is f
 ree\, ADA accessible\, and open to the public. Music in the Art Gallery Up
 coming Artists: November 20 - Linda Warnaar December 18 - Kingdom Mountain
  Dulcimers with Reeve Lindbergh\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:St. Johnsbury Athenaeum\, 1171 Main St.
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/music-in-t
 he-gallery-benjii-aresty-05-10-2026-16-59-46
END:VEVENT
