BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Travelin' McCourys
DTSTART:20261016T190000
DTEND:20261016T210000
DTSTAMP:20261016T152432Z
UID:c2042f8f756ea9f7122e9eb4f73bde@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:From a source deep\, abundant\, and pure the river flows. It
 ’s there on the map\, marking place and time. Yet\, the river changes as
  it remains a constant\, carving away at the edges\, making new pathways\,
  gaining strength as it progresses forward. The Travelin’ McCourys are t
 hat river. The McCoury brothers—Ronnie (mandolin) and Rob (banjo)—were
  born into the bluegrass tradition. Talk about a source abundant and pure:
  their father\, Del\, is among the most influential and successful musicia
 ns in the history of the genre. Years on the road with Dad in the Del McCo
 ury Band honed their knife-edge chops and encouraged the duo to imagine ho
 w traditional bluegrass could cut innovative pathways into 21st century mu
 sic. “If you put your mind\, your skills\, and your ability to it\, I th
 ink you can make just about anything work on bluegrass instruments\,” sa
 ys Ronnie. “That’s a really fun part of this—figuring the new stuff 
 out and surprising the audience.”\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Spruce Peak Arts\, 122 Hourglass Dr.
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/the-travel
 in-mccourys-15-09-2026-16-36-51
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Thunder From Down Under
DTSTART:20261016T190000
DTEND:20261016T210000
DTSTAMP:20261016T152432Z
UID:8fe2b0cf2b752efb39bf179fefaa24@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Age restriction: 18+ No exceptions. Direct from Las Vegas\, th
 e world’s number one male revue\, Australia’s Thunder from Down Under
 \, is hitting the road with their all-new Most Wanted Tour\, bringing the 
 heat across the country and beyond. For more than three decades\, these ic
 onic Aussie exports have been thrilling audiences worldwide with their sig
 nature mix of high-energy stage production\, down-to-earth Aussie charisma
 \, and pure thunder power. With a record-breaking residency at the Excalib
 ur Resort & Casino in Las Vegas\, they have become an international phenom
 enon. Now\, with the Most Wanted Tour\, the Thunder boys are taking their 
 world-famous show across the USA and beyond\, following sold-out tours thr
 oughout Europe\, Asia\, Australia\, and Canada. 30 Center St Rutland \, Ve
 rmont 05701 802-775-0903 boxoffice@paramountvt.org https://www.paramountvt
